  "assessment_at_capture": {
    "escalate": true,
    "severity": "Critical",
    "rationale": "This incident is Critical due to multiple factors, most notably a successful login attempt from a known malicious IP address (198.51.100.77). The evidence shows 10 login attempts, with 9 failures and 1 success, originating from this single IP over a very short span of 0.38 seconds at a high rate (28.88 req/sec). The attack targeted 5 distinct usernames, which, combined with the rapid automated behavior, aligns with a credential stuffing or brute force pattern. The threat intelligence confirms that 198.51.100.77 has a 'malicious' reputation as a 'scanner' and is associated with known host-scanning and brute-force activity. The confirmed malicious source and the success of even one login attempt signify an account compromise, requiring immediate attention beyond normal pipeline processing.",
    "correlation": {
